{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PREMISE FAILURE — do not implement as written (bug-bash triage, no code changed).\n\nThis ticket's prescribed fix ('call await_required_fields at the top of main(), before the agent run begins') is exactly the pre-create call site that bug 941b-f049-5f29-4410 landed to REMOVE, and scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py now bans it in terms: 'SO THE ONLY CORRECT PLACE TO CALL await_required_fields IS AFTER A JIRA SOFTWARE PROJECT HAS BEEN CREATED... Callers must not resurrect a pre-create call site.'\n\nOrdering evidence:\n- 941b (commit 0df44dcbc9) landed AFTER 9790 (2613827564). Run 30981084637 measured that GreenHopper provisions Epic Link/Epic Name on the FIRST Jira Software project create (27 fields / 0 customfield_* before AND after 180s of quiet; 55 fields / both Epic fields 0.0512s after the 201). Waiting before a project exists is a deadlock, not a slow path (runs 30975323866: 62 ERRORS; 30978613228: expired at 1800s).\n- Both surviving call sites are post-create: scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py:186 (after the project POST at :166) and tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py:581 (directly downstream of _create_scratch_project's 201).\n- scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py main() creates NO project before the agent run — it mints a PAT then runs the agent. The project creates are inside the AGENT's own checklist ('for a project created from EACH candidate template (POST /rest/api/2/project)'). So there is nothing before the run that could provision the fields.\n\nConsequence of implementing as written: the wait would burn its full budget on every run and abort with not_ready_message, turning a working workflow_dispatch job into one that can never complete. That is a hard behavior break, the opposite of the intended hardening.\n\nThe underlying concern is still real: a capability-map run can report 'Epic Link absent from this image' when the truth is 'no Software project existed yet'. But the fix cannot be a pre-run gate. Viable directions for a re-scoped ticket:\n  (a) POST-run validation — after the agent's structured answer comes back, if it reports the Epic fields absent AND the recorded inventory has zero customfield_* entries, mark the report UNVERIFIED / fail the job, citing 941b's two-candidate-cause split. This is the discriminator the module already implements (describe_inventory).\n  (b) Have main() create a throwaway Jira Software project itself before the agent run, then call await_required_fields post-create — but that changes what the run maps (the agent's own per-template project creates are the point of step 1), so it needs a deliberate decision.\n  (c) Instruct the agent, in _INSTRUCTIONS_TEMPLATE, to re-read /rest/api/2/field AFTER its first successful project create and to treat a zero-customfield_* inventory as 'not yet provisioned', never as 'absent from this image'.\n\nRecommend re-scoping to (a) and/or (c) — both preserve behavior — before any implementation. No claim taken, no worktree, no code changed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786497953839610001,"uuid":"968bbe20-e9ee-4162-85ca-8e6e4703e83b"}